<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Homebrew on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/homebrew/</link><description>Recent content in Homebrew on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 26 Nov 2008 12:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/homebrew/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Fuzebox, open source gaming</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/fuzebox-open-source-gaming/</link><pubDate>Wed, 26 Nov 2008 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/fuzebox-open-source-gaming/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 2 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 18 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.bloglines.com/"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Take me back to my 8bit gaming youth? &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;a name="base9477167"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;table id="table9477167" bg cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" width="100%" style="color:#bde0ed;"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt; &lt;td rowspan="2"&gt; &lt;table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;span class="blogtitle"&gt;&lt;a href="http://pipes.yahoo.com/pipes/pipe.info?_id=8IsQFi282xG5FaTJJjBjOg"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Life GH Com&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Pipes Output &lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;a name="base9477167"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;div id="items9477167" style="display: block;"&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr bgcolor="#ffffff"&gt; &lt;td&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a title="Site: Life GH Com" href="http://hackaday.com/2008/11/25/fuzebox-open-source-gaming/"&gt;Fuzebox, open source gaming&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="snap_preview"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img class="alignnone size-full wp-image-6283" title="fuzebox" src="http://hackadaycom.files.wordpress.com/2008/11/fuzebox.jpg?w=450&amp;amp;h=289" alt="fuzebox" height="289" width="450" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adafruit has just put their &lt;a rel="nofollow" title="Uzebox - The ATMega Game Console" target="_blank" href="http://belogic.com/uzebox/"&gt;Uzebox&lt;/a&gt; based console into production. The &lt;a rel="nofollow" title="Adafruit Industries, Unique &amp;amp; fun DIY electronics and kits" target="_blank" href="http://www.adafruit.com/index.php?main_page=index&amp;amp;cPath=30"&gt;Fuzebox&lt;/a&gt; is an 8bit game console based around the ATmega644-20PU microcontroller. Full 256 color 240×224 resolution video output is provide by either a composite connection or svideo. There is an SD card slot on board for future expansion. The chip takes care of all the I/O, so you just need to write your game code in C on top of it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The kit looks &lt;a rel="nofollow" title="Fuzebox - Build the Box" target="_blank" href="http://www.ladyada.net/make/fuzebox/solder.html"&gt;easy to assemble&lt;/a&gt;. Almost all of the components are through-hole. The video chip is SMD and comes presoldered to the board. The kit has two SNES controller ports included, but you can use NES ports too. There are three ways you can load your program onto the board: 6pin FTDI, ICSP10, and ICSP6.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://feeds.wordpress.com/1.0/gocomments/hackadaycom.wordpress.com/6282/"&gt;&lt;img alt="" src="http://feeds.wordpress.com/1.0/comments/hackadaycom.wordpress.com/6282/" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://feeds.wordpress.com/1.0/godelicious/hackadaycom.wordpress.com/6282/"&gt;&lt;img alt="" src="http://feeds.wordpress.com/1.0/delicious/hackadaycom.wordpress.com/6282/" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://feeds.wordpress.com/1.0/gostumble/hackadaycom.wordpress.com/6282/"&gt;&lt;img alt="" src="http://feeds.wordpress.com/1.0/stumble/hackadaycom.wordpress.com/6282/" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://feeds.wordpress.com/1.0/godigg/hackadaycom.wordpress.com/6282/"&gt;&lt;img alt="" src="http://feeds.wordpress.com/1.0/digg/hackadaycom.wordpress.com/6282/" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://feeds.wordpress.com/1.0/goreddit/hackadaycom.wordpress.com/6282/"&gt;&lt;img alt="" src="http://feeds.wordpress.com/1.0/reddit/hackadaycom.wordpress.com/6282/" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img alt="" src="http://stats.wordpress.com/b.gif?host=hackaday.com&amp;amp;blog=4779443&amp;amp;post=6282&amp;amp;subd=hackadaycom&amp;amp;ref=&amp;amp;feed=1" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td align="left" valign="top"&gt; &lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt; &lt;td align="right" valign="top"&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Nintendo DS Homebrew</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/nintendo-ds-homebrew/</link><pubDate>Thu, 13 Nov 2008 10:39:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/nintendo-ds-homebrew/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 4 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 8 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a onblur="try {parent.deselectBloggerImageGracefully();} catch(e) {}" href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEh5xqG0v9vbKwtJsUqPN6a8uqPgjKzcp5Hqr5IXkh21FZ7dN7q7R8ewZYQiTYVLwSjeq14Y8H8qooWh0GlPHiedIpdR-OnUY7P1o220ryWUA3Kj_OZF2WNiAPnJvsSr1VT4IFX3GueSIEw/s1600-h/Nintendo_DS_Lite_Black_Console.jpg"&gt;&lt;img style="margin: 0pt 10px 10px 0pt; float: left; cursor: pointer; width: 200px; height: 200px;" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEh5xqG0v9vbKwtJsUqPN6a8uqPgjKzcp5Hqr5IXkh21FZ7dN7q7R8ewZYQiTYVLwSjeq14Y8H8qooWh0GlPHiedIpdR-OnUY7P1o220ryWUA3Kj_OZF2WNiAPnJvsSr1VT4IFX3GueSIEw/s200/Nintendo_DS_Lite_Black_Console.jpg" alt="" id="BLOGGER_PHOTO_ID_5268090940044084994" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;I&amp;rsquo;ve been getting extremely excited about the Nintendo DS home brew scene. The &lt;a href="http://tinyurl.com/5t86zh"&gt;Spectrum&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="http://tinyurl.com/5jbpbc"&gt;SNES&lt;/a&gt; emulators look like a win, also there is a &lt;a href="http://tinyurl.com/6n6q3j"&gt;Doom&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="http://quake.drunkencoders.com/"&gt;Quake&lt;/a&gt; port available. Happy days&amp;hellip;&amp;hellip;..&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle&amp;rsquo;s Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>